text = "Note: This documentation will be messy.
[font_size=18]Data:[/font_size]
Data is simple, its an array of dicts with values in them that can either be used externally or used for searching/sorting.
[font_size=18]Search Scheme:[/font_size]
The way search behaves, this makes use of tokens and weight (tokens are just the input string split by spaces)
[code]{
	\"data_key\":{
		\"type\":<contains/exact (see below)>,
		\"weight\":3
		\"token_weight\":0.5
		\"position_weight\":1
	}
}[/code]
[font_size=16]Types[/font_size]
\"contains\": checks if any of the input tokens are within any of the value tokens
\"exact\": checks if any of the input tokens exactly match any of the value tokens
\"range\": this is unfinished and idk why it exists (supposed to handle dates but it don't have code)
[font_size=16]Weights[/font_size]
\"weight\": this weight is added the first time a token matches
\"token_weight\": this weight is added per token match
\"position_weight\": this weight is multiplied by how far to the left this token match is in the input string (this[5x] is[4x] how[3x] it[2x] works[1x])
[font_size=18]Sort Scheme:[/font_size]
(you have to press 'Update UI' to access sorting in the sort dropdown)
Sorting uses groups, each sort rule pass will only effect data in each group, not across groups. (excluding \"group\")
[code]{
	\"sort_mode\":{
		\"data_key\":{
				\"type\":<sort/order/group (see below)>
			}
	}
}[/code]
[font_size=16]Types[/font_size]
\"sort\": Re-orders data in each group from a to z use \"reverse\":true to sort from z to a
\"order\": Split current groups into groups in order of data values defined in \"order\":[\"data to check for\",\"data that's below it\"] use \"reverse\":true to reverse the order, data values that are not in the list are always at the bottom no matter what.
\"group\": Merges data with the same data value into new groups keeping order, user \"reverse\":true to reverse the newly created groups only.
[font_size=16]Extra[/font_size]
Use \"reverse_after\":true to reverse all data after the rule gets applied"

